{
    "background_story": "Harlem grew up in a small beach town, where his family owned a quaint cabana rental business. As a child, he spent his summers playing in the sand and helping his parents with the cabanas. As he got older, Harlem took a keen interest in architecture and design. He decided to study abroad, where he honed his skills in sustainable and eco-friendly building practices. After completing his studies, Harlem returned to his hometown and transformed the family business into a luxurious eco-resort. The cabanas were redesigned with reclaimed wood, solar panels, and lush green roofs. Harlem's passion project quickly gained popularity among environmentally-conscious travelers. His cabanas became a symbol of his love for the ocean and his commitment to preserving the natural beauty of his hometown.",
